WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.890
What the Friendship Cup stands 
for is definitely wrong.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.350
But even knowing that, I couldn't do anything.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.250
Just then, Tsukikage, who'd been 
sent underground, appeared.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:18.220
It turned out Tsukikage let himself be sent 
underground on Reiji Akaba's orders,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.930
in order to gather information.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.230
Tsukikage also gave me a message from Layra.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.110
We came here to save this world.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.830
But no one in this dimension believes that.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.250
They don't believe in the power of the Lancers.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.850
To make them believe,

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.440
we have to beat Jack!

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.590
I'll win!

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.240
With my style of dueling!

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.450
And I'll bring true smiles back to 
the hearts of City's people!

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.580
D-Wheels.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.830
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.490
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.140
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.140
The Clown's Mask

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.430
It's time for the first round's last duel.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.810
Fighting will be... Syun Kurosaki!

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.790
His opponent... Dennis Mackfield!

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.870
Damn you... Are you really from LDS?

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.800
That's right. Why do you ask?

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.490
The practical battle skills he showed back then...

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.510
He certainly didn't learn them at LDS.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:25.570
He probably suspects something.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.410
I'd better crush him thoroughly this time...

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.790
Thoroughly.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.120
Kurosaki and Dennis...

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.500
Members of the Lancers have 
to crush each other?

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.200
You may be dissatisfied with this match-up.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.170
It's an important match for us 
to watch. Right, chairman?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.370
Yes.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.390
I'm not dissatisfied at all.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.580
I'm very interested in the match's 
outcome, as well.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.390
Go, Kurosaki!

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:05.090
Show us you're number one above ground, too!

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:10.030
Kurosaki, the number one most popular 
duelist in underground dueling,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.970
will face the entertainer Dennis, who gained 
popularity doing shows in Central Park!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.600
He's even cuter than he looked on TV!

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.660
City's people, who are filled with friendship,

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.860
I will show you my dazzling illusions.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.550
It's show time!

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.550
The duel between these two

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:42.330
is truly an appropriate match to close 
the first round of the Friendship Cup.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.080
I bet not a single person is saying,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.760
"Don't get your hopes up here!"

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.030
What kind of battle are we about to see?

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.220
I'm so excited to find out!

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.800
It stinks that we have to fight amongst 
ourselves, but let's fight hard, okay?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.670
I'll use this duel to figure out if we 
really are on the same team.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.520
Aw, so mean...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.220
Okay, let's go! Action Field, on!

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.690
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration!

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.290
Duel mode, on.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.840
Autopilot, stand by.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.940
Riding duel...

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.170
Acceleration!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.780
Duel!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.850
I'll expose what you really are!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.950
He broke away!

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.330
The first to the corner is Kurosaki.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.690
He takes the first turn!

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:48.380
I summon Raidraptor — Skull 
Eagle from my hand.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:55.180
And I activate my spell card Raidraptor — Call.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.900
It lets me Special Summon another monster 
with the same name from my deck.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.510
I overlay my two Skull Eagles!

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.720
Xyz Summon!

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.870
Come out, Rank 3 Raidraptor — Fiend Eagle!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.640
The king of the underground duel

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.930
completes an Xyz Summon, first thing!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.670
The monster effect of the Skull Eagles, 
used as components, activates!

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.390
For each one, Fiend Eagle's attack 
points increase by 300.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.840
And I activate Fiend Eagle's monster effect.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.710
I use one Overlay Unit to deal damage 
to you equal to the attack points

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.690
of one monster on my field!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.990
Big damage to Dennis, right off the bat!

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.720
That again?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.460
What do you mean by "again"?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.130
My mind-reading magic!

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:00.200
You have a Rank-Up-Magic in your hand.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.170
I activate Rank-Up-Magic Raid 
Force from my hand!

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.010
You're going to activate it on your 
next turn, just like last time,

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.240
to summon a powerful monster, right?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.260
Looks like he was right!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.020
That's pretty amazing!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.220
He can see right through to my heart!

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.450
Seriously, don't fall into clichés.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.620
You're making the show less exciting.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:28.540
You...

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.060
An entertainment show has to have surprises.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:37.430
Trying to provoke your opponent, to put 
yourself in an advantageous position?

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.170
That's a combat tactic they don't teach at LDS.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.470
Is that a compliment?

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:45.940
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.100
My turn... Draw!

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.290
This, huh?

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.090
What are you trying to get me to do? Seriously...

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.170
Now, following my mind-reading magic,

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.560
I'll demonstrate the grand trick of the era!

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.790
Fiend Eagle's Overlay Unit...

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.270
My, my!

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.860
Oh, dear...

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.420
Has Performage Cup Tricker 
always been there?

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.540
Just kidding.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.620
I can use one Overlay Unit from 
an Xyz Monster on the field

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.790
to Special Summon Cup Tricker from my hand.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.990
How dare you steal one of my 
monster's Overlay Units?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.350
But there's more to come!

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:40.700
I now lower the attack points 
of my target monster,

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.730
in other words, Fiend Eagle, by 600.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.200
Damn.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.250
Next, a spell card. Magical Pendulum Box.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.680
Its effect lets me draw two cards!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.540
And if I draw a Pendulum Monster, 
I add it to my hand.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.360
If not, I send it to the graveyard.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.920
Wow! Both are Pendulums!

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:10.680
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Performage Bonus Dealer

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:15.600
and Scale 6 Performage Overlay Juggler!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.180
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 5 simultaneously.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.700
Pendulum Summon!

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:29.270
Come out, my Performages!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.990
First, Performage Wind Drainer.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:37.690
Then, Performage Wing Sandwichman.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.390
And last, Performage Ball Balancer!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:46.630
Dennis unleashes the Pendulum Summon he 
first unveiled in his street performance!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:50.070
Three Level 5 monsters? Going to Xyz?

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:54.210
Hold your horses... The show's just started.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.990
I activate Bonus Dealer's Pendulum Effect.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:01.580
When I Pendulum Summon three or 
more Performages from my hand,

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.650
I draw two cards!

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:09.920
I Normal Summon Performage Fire Dancer.

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:14.860
I overlay Level 4 Ball Balancer and Fire Dancer!

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.630
The show must go on!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:27.400
Sky magician, travel around 
the stage magnificently!

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:29.210
Xyz Summon!

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.580
Come out, Rank 4 Performage Trapeze Magician!

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:40.890
This is incredible! Dennis performed 
an Xyz Summon, too!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.960
The first Xyz battle in the history 
of the Friendship Cup!

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.090
A truly heart-pounding development, 
worthy of the round's last match!

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.860
But so far, it's the same as last time.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.480
Why not show your true self already?

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:59.100
Stop worrying! My show isn't over yet!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.250
I overlay Level 5 Cup Tricker,

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:07.020
Wind Drainer, and Wing Sandwichman!

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.580
Descend, performer of the demon world!

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.620
Xyz Summon!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.770
Rank 5 Performage Shadow Maker!

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:25.030
I activate Trapeze Magician's effect, 
targeting Shadow Maker.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.770
I use one Overlay Unit

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.740
to allow Shadow Maker to 
attack twice in one turn!

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:37.040
And as an effect target, Shadow Maker's 
effect activates!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.280
I use one Overlay Unit

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:44.180
to Special Summon a second 
Shadow Maker from my deck.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:56.190
And the effect of Cup Tricker,

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:00.090
sent to the graveyard as an Overlay Unit, activates!

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:08.400
Its effect lets me transfer the Overlay Unit of 
one Xyz Monster on the field to another.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:13.040
And using Trapeze Magician's 
other Overlay Unit,

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:17.370
I allow the second Shadow Maker 
to attack twice, too.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:22.710
Now, I use the Overlay Units on 
the second Shadow Maker,

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.490
to Special Summon a third Shadow Maker!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.200
Incredible! A fourth Xyz Monster 
is summoned to Dennis's field!

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:35.320
And two of those can attack twice.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.270
Which means his total attack points are...

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.670
15,500?!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:47.740
Battle! I attack Fiend Eagle with Trapeze Magician!

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:59.690
In that instant, I activate my Continuous 
Trap, targeting Trapeze Magician!

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.390
Raidraptor — Target Flag!

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:11.370
I draw one card, and we both check it.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.370
The card is Raidraptor — Last 
Strix, a monster card.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:21.370
When my target, Trapeze Magician, 
leaves the field,

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:26.200
it destroys Target Flag, and then 
I check your hand.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:33.360
If you have a card in your hand of the 
same type as the one I drew—

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:38.330
in other words, a monster card—I destroy 
it, sending it to the graveyard.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.250
But it won't matter.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.770
You're about to run out of life!

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.670
I still have more battle to go.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.580
I activate my Quick-Play Spell Rank-Up-Magic 
Doom Double Force!

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:54.730
I Special Summon the destroyed 
Rank 3 Fiend Eagle...

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.380
And overlay it!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.740
I Special Summon a Raidraptor 
with double its rank.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.790
Proud falcon, flap your wings that are 
stained with the blood of heroes,

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.330
and travel the path of revolution!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:13.500
Rank Up Xyz Change!

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:19.790
Appear, Rank 6 Raidraptor — Revolution Falcon!

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.540
I-Incredible. He used a destroyed 
monster to Xyz Summon!

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.750
I activate its monster effect!

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:32.490
When Revolution Falcon uses a Raidraptor 
as a rank-up component,

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.690
I can destroy one monster that my 
opponent Special Summoned,

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.600
dealing half its attack points as damage.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:42.390
Use the flame of revolution 
to reveal his true self.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:45.110
I destroy Trapeze Magician!

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:52.600
I can't have that... Trapeze Magician 
is the symbol of my show.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.700
I activate the effect of Performage 
Magic Tactician in my hand.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.940
When a monster on my side of the 
field is targeted by an effect,

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:04.640
I can send this card and one from 
my field to the graveyard.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.720
Then, I switch your monster's effect 
target to another monster.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:22.870
Shadow Maker is destroyed, but Trapeze 
Magician's effect lets me avoid damage!

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.840
I managed to keep Trapeze Magician safe.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.040
Now, I end my turn.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:34.970
After all, even if I try attacking with 
Special Summoned monsters,

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:40.120
Revolution Falcon's effect will render 
their attack points 0, right?

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.250
What's with this duel?

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.900
Show his true self?

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.230
"True self." What does Kurosaki mean by that?

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:58.470
You mean to hide your true self till the end?

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.560
What true self do you mean?

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.170
My show contains no tricks or plants!

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:16.880
My turn!

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.160
I activate Revolution Falcon's effect.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:24.060
I use one Overlay Unit to 
attack all of your monsters.

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.260
Battle! First, I destroy Trapeze Magician!

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.500
I told you, I can't have that!

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:34.070
Revolutional Air Raid!

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.940
Action Spell Battle Change.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:43.280
During a battle declared on your turn, I can 
choose your monster's attack target.

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.250
What?

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.450
I change Revolution Falcon's attack target

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:49.420
from Trapeze Magician to Shadow Maker!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.310
But as you know,

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:57.290
when Revolution Falcon battles a 
Special Summoned monster,

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:00.260
that monster's attack and defense 
points become 0.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:11.940
Too bad... Overlay Juggler's Pendulum Effect

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:16.340
transferred Shadow Maker's Overlay 
Unit to Trapeze Magician.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.730
You're only prolonging the inevitable.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.620
Have you forgotten that I can 
attack all your monsters?

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.210
Go, Revolution Falcon.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.830
Attack Trapeze Magician!

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.800
Revolutional Air Raid!

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.730
I've seen a duel like this before.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.130
I don't intend to enjoy your duel.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.210
To me, this is a battlefield!

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.300
It's just like that time...

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:00.280
Trapeze Magician!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:08.700
At last, Dennis's ace monster, 
Trapeze Magician is destroyed.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.350
Then, Dennis's life is...

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:12.120
What?

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:16.910
Even though an attack-position monster 
was destroyed, he didn't lose any life?

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.160
How?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:22.110
I activated my Action Spell Damage Banish.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:26.980
In its last moments, Trapeze gave that to me.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:33.500
That card reduced battle damage to 0.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:34.930
Though only once.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.900
You just barely managed to hang in there.

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:41.780
But your show ends now!

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.630
Continuous Trap Target Flag's effect activates.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:49.320
When Trapeze Magician leaves the 
field, Target Flag is destroyed!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.910
And I force you to reveal your hand!

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.520
Now, show your true self!

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.340
Is this what you wanted to see?

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.850
Polymerization?

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.170
I knew it.

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:06.360
Now, use that card!

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:10.140
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.770
Then, let me show you the 
ultimate in entertainment.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:17.870
My turn...

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:19.500
Draw!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:28.210
I activate my spell card Chaos 
Ancient Gear Fusion.

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:30.680
I send Polymerization from my 
hand to the graveyard,

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:36.140
and banish Xyz Monsters in my graveyard equal 
to the number of fusion components I need!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:43.020
Then, I can Special Summon a set of fusion 
components from my deck and Extra Deck,

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:46.760
negating their effects and summon requirements!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.100
Ancient Gear Hunting Hound, 
Double Ancient Gear Hunting Hound,

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:54.970
Triple Ancient Gear Hunting Hound, 
Ultimate Ancient Gear Hunting Hound!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:59.940
I Special Summon a total of 
four Ancient Gear monsters!

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.550
Ancient Gear...

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:16.810
He's...

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.470
I fuse the four Ancient Gears!

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:24.800
Mechanical hunting dogs, 
inheriting the souls of antiquity,

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:30.390
bring your ten heads together and 
achieve the power of chaos!

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:34.910
Fusion Summon!

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:40.990
Appear, Level 10 Chaos Ancient Gear Giant!

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:02.880
I-It's huge.

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:06.070
Wh-Wh-What is this?!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.380
Such a huge monster...

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:11.620
That's...

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.800
It seems you've seen it somewhere before...

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:30.170
So you really are with Academia!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.240
What is the meaning of this?

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:36.940
Explain it to us.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:40.640
Explain? How could I?

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:44.700
Isn't Academia your enemy?

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.620
Why is there an enemy in your ranks?

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:51.920
I'd foreseen the possibility of hostiles 
infiltrating the Lancers' ranks.

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:55.530
But what about you?

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:58.800
Dennis summoned an incredible 
Level 10 monster!

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:03.220
It's enormous, with 4500 attack points!

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:09.720
Now, it's time for the hunting game.

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:48.070
It can't be. Dennis is from Academia?

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:52.320
I won't let that terrible giant run rampant again.

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:56.860
But if you could have stopped it, 
wouldn't Heartland still be at peace?

00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:57.720
Shut up!

00:23:57.720 --> 00:24:02.780
With iron strength and steel 
will, I will crush you!

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:06.990
I'll see that you receive a reward 
for removing my mask...

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:11.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Rebel's Curse.

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.270
The fun is only getting started!
